sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor User
  participant PI as processUserInput()
  participant QE as QueryEngine
  participant QC as query()
  participant CTX as system/user context builders
  participant API as services/api/claude.ts
  participant Model as Anthropic model
  participant TR as tool runtime
  participant ST as AppState / task state

  par Direct user input
    User->>PI: prompt / slash command / attachment
  and Background event
    ST-->>PI: hook / task / remote notification
  and Background agent completion
    ST-->>QE: task completion message
  end

  PI->>PI: resolve command, attachments, hooks
  PI->>QE: append internal Message objects
  QE->>QC: submitMessage()

  QC->>CTX: build systemPrompt + userContext + systemContext
  CTX-->>QC: normalized prompt prefix
  QC->>API: normalizeMessagesForAPI() + build request
  API->>Model: stream conversation turn

  loop until stop / compact / error
    Model-->>API: assistant text / tool_use / stop signal
    API-->>QC: stream event

    alt assistant text only
      QC->>QE: append assistant Message
    else tool_use blocks
      QC->>TR: permission check
      TR->>TR: toolOrchestration / StreamingToolExecutor
      TR->>ST: side effects (fs / shell / mcp / network)
      TR-->>QC: tool_result / progress / synthetic error
      QC->>QE: append tool_result Message
      QC->>ST: update AppState / task state / permissions
      QC->>API: send updated transcript for next turn
    else stop / recovery / compaction
      QC->>ST: update budgets / compact state / recovery state
      QC->>QE: append control messages if needed
    end
  end

  Note over QE,ST: The loop is message-driven, not function-call-driven.\nEvery new event is converted into messages, then fed back into the next model turn.
